# Bag fees
All published bag fees apply at each check-in location and are base rates according to travel dates and destination; applicable taxes are not shown.

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0003; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0001; source-lines: 2-2; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
```


## Carry-on bags
You're allowed 1 carry-on bag and 1 personal item in all cabins.

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0004; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0002; source-lines: 5-5; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
```


### Personal items
Your personal item like a purse or small handbag must fit under the seat in front of you. Dimensions should not exceed 18 x 14 x 8 inches (45 x 35 x 20 cm).

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0005; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0003; source-lines: 8-8; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
```


These don't count as your personal item or carry-on:
* Diaper bags (1 per child)
* Breast pump
* Small, soft-sided cooler of breast milk
* Child safety seats, strollers and medical or mobility devices

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0006; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0004; source-lines: 10-14; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
```


### Carry-on items
You can bring only one carry-on item along with your personal item. Your carry-on must fit in in the overhead bin or under the seat in front of you. If it doesn't fit, it will need to be checked. Be sure all your carry-on items are labeled in case they are checked.

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0007; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0005; source-lines: 17-17; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
```


#### Carry-on bag
The total size of your carry-on, including the handles and wheels, cannot exceed 22 x 14 x 9 inches (56 x 36 x 23 cm) and must fit in the sizer at the airport.

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0008; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0006; source-lines: 20-20; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
```


#### Soft-sided garment bag
Your soft-sided garment bag cannot exceed 51 inches / 130 cm (length + width + height).

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0009; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0007; source-lines: 23-23; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
```


## Checked bags
Bag fees have been updated effective for tickets issued on / after February 20, 2024.

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0010; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0008; source-lines: 26-26; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
```


Travel within / between the U.S., Puerto Rico, and U.S. Virgin Islands – 1st checked bag fee is $40 and the 2nd checked bag fee is $45.

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0011; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0009; source-lines: 28-28; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
```


Travel to / from Canada, Caribbean, Mexico, Central America, and Guyana – 1st checked bag fee is $35 and the 2nd checked bag fee is $45.

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0012; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0010; source-lines: 30-30; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
```


All bag fees are non-refundable and apply per person, each way, even if you buy or get an upgrade that includes free checked bags. If you believe you were incorrectly charged for bag fees, contact an American representative for help or file a refund claim within 45 days.

<!-- rtdf-block-id: airline/section1_non_textual:b0013; role: provision; provision-id: airline/section1_non_textual:p0011; source-lines: 32-32; relation: formalizes-preceding -->
```catala
```


